    "Existing v10 image landmarks are retained exactly for registration to immutable anchors, without changing commercial geometry. Source image is 2150x1850; controls are in the pre-existing 1696x1459 reduced coordinate space.",
    "height_mm and width_mm are HALF section extents in-plane and transverse respectively, not full diameters. Sections, hidden depths and blend radii are exterior visual estimates.",
    "Upper and lower long runs use straight segments with only short local corner blends. The real Force retains a dipped top-tube junction and lower/head elbows; it must not inherit CAPRA straightness indiscriminately.",
    "gt_upper_brace closes the characteristic upper triangular window between seat column and top-tube valley; retain open interior rather than filling triangle.",
    "Chainstay begins at the separate rear suspension joint near [272,894], not at rear axle [183,863]. Rear dropout adapters connect these two joints; do not turn it into a bowed continuous generic chainstay.",
    "Rocker outer/hole contours follow lateral manufacturer photo and dedicated High Pivot LTS closeup. Three bearing centers are rear joint [665,706], fixed frame pivot [806,699] and moving upper shock joint [920,626]. Opposite plate/depth inferred from official oblique image.",
    "Lower shock eye fixed cradle follows [829,904]. Upper eye belongs to moving rocker; do not add fixed frame bar to upper shock eye.",
